<html>
<body style="font-family: -apple-system, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;">
<h2>Welcome to the Wild Jag Plugins installer</h2>
<p>On the next screen, use the checkboxes to choose which plugins to install, and within each plugin which formats (Audio Unit, VST3, Standalone App):</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Caverns</b> v__CAVERNS_VERSION__ - reverb/delay</li>
<li><b>Damage</b> v__DAMAGE_VERSION__ - fuzz/distortion</li>
<li><b>Corrosion</b> v__CORROSION_VERSION__ - lo-fi drive</li>
<li><b>Flux</b> v__FLUX_VERSION__ - analog phase shifter</li>
<li><b>Alloy</b> v__ALLOY_VERSION__ - industrial bass synth</li>
<li><b>Gradient</b> v__GRADIENT_VERSION__ - pitch shifting delay</li>
<li><b>Shields</b> v__SHIELDS_VERSION__ - diffuse reverb</li>
<li><b>Intruder</b> v__INTRUDER_VERSION__ - non-linear gated reverb</li>
<li><b>Strike</b> v__STRIKE_VERSION__ - Karplus-Strong physical-modeling string synth</li>
</ul>
<p>You'll also be asked whether to install for all users of this Mac (<code>/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins</code>, <code>/Applications</code> - requires an administrator password) or just for you (<code>~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins</code>, <code>~/Applications</code> - no password needed). Both are locations every AU/VST3 host scans.</p>
<p>Restart your DAW (or run AU validation) after installing so it picks up the new plugins.</p>
</body>
</html>
